but I'll get into the details.

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:55.081
- I wanna hear that story,
and then I also wanna know

00:04:55.081 --> 00:04:56.961
what dating advice you have for women

00:04:56.961 --> 00:04:58.517
in their 20's in New York City.

00:04:58.517 --> 00:05:00.142
(laughter)

00:05:00.142 --> 00:05:01.698
- Oh, god, this is great.

00:05:01.698 --> 00:05:02.859
- We've never talked about this.

00:05:02.859 --> 00:05:04.124
- Listen, you're absolutely right.

00:05:04.124 --> 00:05:05.517
I've never talked about this.

00:05:05.517 --> 00:05:09.440
Um, so, the legend is, and it's true,

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.693
that after Lizzie and I's first date,

00:05:11.693 --> 00:05:13.876
which was a three hour date

00:05:13.876 --> 00:05:16.023
on a Sunday night in New York City.

00:05:16.023 --> 00:05:17.080
Which, little fun fact,

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.077
the Jets happened to win that Sunday,

00:05:19.077 --> 00:05:21.781
and had they lost the date
would have not happened.

00:05:21.781 --> 00:05:22.815
So that just--

00:05:22.815 --> 00:05:23.918
- You would have cancelled?

00:05:23.918 --> 00:05:24.997
- It's, I would have cancelled.

00:05:24.997 --> 00:05:26.135
- Because you would have been upset, okay.

00:05:26.135 --> 00:05:27.179
- Yeah, that's exactly right,

00:05:27.179 --> 00:05:27.829
- Okay.

00:05:27.829 --> 00:05:29.119
(laughter)

00:05:29.119 --> 00:05:29.943
- It went extremely well.

00:05:29.943 --> 00:05:31.244
I lived in Jersey by the Wine Library,

00:05:31.244 --> 00:05:32.416
she lived on the Upper East Side.

00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:35.260
I drove her home, and I dropped her off

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.197
and two minutes after I dropped her off

00:05:38.197 --> 00:05:39.881
I called her on her cell phone,

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:41.483
she wasn't even in her apartment

00:05:41.483 --> 00:05:45.116
and my opening line was,
can you believe this is it?

00:05:45.116 --> 00:05:46.417
And that was it.

00:05:46.417 --> 00:05:48.645
And we talked from that moment all the way

00:05:48.645 --> 00:05:49.725
to my 45 minute drive home,

00:05:49.725 --> 00:05:51.780
and until like four
o'clock in the morning.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.462
And we we're married within
the year of our first date.

00:05:54.462 --> 00:05:56.423
So, that's the legend of that story.

00:05:56.423 --> 00:05:59.279
Little tears from the ladies
in the audience. I love it.

00:05:59.279 --> 00:06:03.435
Ah, advice, so you know I think about.

00:06:03.435 --> 00:06:05.083
It's really funny, having a daughter

00:06:05.083 --> 00:06:08.195
changes so much in a man's life, I think.

00:06:08.195 --> 00:06:10.203
And so, though I know she's gonna grow up

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.213
in a very different world,

00:06:11.213 --> 00:06:12.537
I sometimes project what,

00:06:12.537 --> 00:06:15.915
and having so many
amazing 20 year old girls

00:06:15.915 --> 00:06:18.678
that work at VaynerMedia,
it's an interesting thing.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.001
Look, I think we're living through

00:06:20.001 --> 00:06:21.453
a really interesting time, right.

00:06:21.453 --> 00:06:25.934
For example, girls are always in a place

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.779
where they're judged by other girls.

00:06:27.779 --> 00:06:30.717
That's the psychology that's
most fascinating to me.

00:06:30.717 --> 00:06:33.677
What would women do in a world where

00:06:33.677 --> 00:06:37.113
that wasn't such an
overwhelming kind of pillar

00:06:37.113 --> 00:06:39.458
to the way they have to
navigate through their lives.

00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:42.337
You know, you can look at
how girls dress on Halloween,

00:06:42.337 --> 00:06:44.531
and like watching all the
comments on Instagram.

00:06:44.531 --> 00:06:46.853
Because these are the
kinda things I look into.

00:06:46.853 --> 00:06:49.454
I would say this, I would say,

00:06:49.454 --> 00:06:51.891
I'm gonna give advice the way
I like to give business advice

00:06:51.891 --> 00:06:54.016
which is think about legacy,

00:06:54.016 --> 00:06:56.976
meaning, I think the world's
changing quite a bit, right.

00:06:56.976 --> 00:06:58.834
Like, you know, there's a lot of talk

00:06:58.834 --> 00:07:01.155
about women in the work place
and the lean in moverment

00:07:01.155 --> 00:07:02.189
and all these things.

00:07:02.189 --> 00:07:04.151
Women are clearly closing the gap.

00:07:04.151 --> 00:07:05.798
You know, the world's changing so much,

00:07:05.798 --> 00:07:07.377
especially in the context of the U.S.

00:07:07.377 --> 00:07:11.209
that I would be more
aggressive, believe it or not.

00:07:11.209 --> 00:07:12.892
That would be my advice, and I know it's

00:07:12.892 --> 00:07:14.656
a little bit of a, kinda a left turn,

00:07:14.656 --> 00:07:18.372
and maybe it's a guy
giving advice to a girl.

00:07:18.372 --> 00:07:20.833
But, like, for me I think it's never been

00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:23.131
more appropriate to be on the offense,

00:07:23.131 --> 00:07:25.696
you know because of just
what's going on in the world.

00:07:25.696 --> 00:07:28.773
And so I think, you
know, I think that women

00:07:28.773 --> 00:07:30.676
are in a much better place than they were

00:07:30.676 --> 00:07:32.767
20 or 30 or 40 years ago to say

00:07:32.767 --> 00:07:35.506
I'm attracted or intrigued
by that gentleman

00:07:35.506 --> 00:07:37.213
and go on the offense.

00:07:37.213 --> 00:07:38.211
You got it Alex.

00:07:38.211 --> 00:07:40.487
And, ah, and that's what I would say.

00:07:40.487 --> 00:07:44.852
I think one of the biggest
mistakes guys and girls make

00:07:44.852 --> 00:07:46.952
is they're just scared
to go in for the move

00:07:46.952 --> 00:07:49.426
because they wanna protect and
hedge against their feelings.

00:07:49.426 --> 00:07:51.875
And I will tell you this, your feelings

00:07:51.875 --> 00:07:53.466
could hurt for a little bit,

00:07:53.466 --> 00:07:55.729
but the long term regret,

00:07:55.729 --> 00:07:57.609
the amount of people who
are watching this right now,

00:07:57.609 --> 00:07:59.943
maybe even in this room that are sad,

00:07:59.943 --> 00:08:02.463
men and women, that they didn't go for it

00:08:02.463 --> 00:08:05.307
and didn't make the move, and didn't try

00:08:05.307 --> 00:08:09.559
that regret is a hell of a
lot longer and more painful

00:08:09.559 --> 00:08:12.565
and more drawn out than
the instant rejection

00:08:12.565 --> 00:08:14.179
of going for it.

00:08:14.179 --> 00:08:16.338
And so I would say a
little bit more aggression.

00:08:16.338 --> 00:08:17.383
- Okay.

00:08:17.383 --> 00:08:18.358
- Cool.

00:08:18.358 --> 00:08:19.322
Awesome.

00:08:19.322 --> 00:08:20.100
Let's move on.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:20.851
